            modern web development while maintaining simplicity and             
            flexibility.\\n\\n## Features\\n\\n1. **URL Routing with Variable   
            Segments and HTTP Method Filtering**\\n   - Support for dynamic URL 
            patterns like `/user/<int:id>`\\n   - HTTP method filtering (GET,   
            POST, PUT, DELETE, etc.)\\n   - Flexible route matching with type   
            converters\\n\\n2. **Request Object**\\n   - Encapsulates HTTP      
            method, path, headers, query string, and body\\n   - Easy access to 
            form data and JSON payloads\\n   - Comprehensive request information
            parsing\\n\\n3. **Response Object**\\n   - Configurable status      
            codes, headers, and body content\\n   - Support for various response
            types (HTML, JSON, etc.)\\n   - Cookie management\\n\\n4. **Jinja2  
            Template Rendering**\\n   - Integrated template engine with         
            application context\\n   - Template inheritance and includes\\n   - 
            Automatic HTML escaping for security\\n\\n5. **Application Context  
            Management**\\n   - Thread-local storage for `current_app` and `g`  
            objects\\n   - Safe concurrent request handling\\n   - Context-aware
            template rendering\\n\\n6. **Blueprint-based Modular                
            Applications**\\n   - Organize routes into reusable blueprints\\n   
            - URL prefix inheritance\\n   - Modular application                 
            architecture\\n\\n## Installation\\n\\n```bash\\npip install -e     
            .\\n```\\n\\n## Quick Start\\n\\n### Basic                          
            Application\\n\\n```python\\nfrom flaskframework import             
            Flask\\n\\napp = Flask(__name__)\\n\\n@app.route(\'/\')\\ndef       
            hello():\\n    return \'Hello,                                      
            World!\'\\n\\n@app.route(\'/user/<name>\')\\ndef user(name):\\n     
            return f\'Hello, {name}!\'\\n\\n@app.route(\'/api/data\',           
            methods=[\'POST\'])\\ndef api_data():\\n    return {\'status\':     
            \'success\'}\\n\\nif __name__ == \'__main__\':\\n                   
            app.run(debug=True)\\n```\\n\\n### Using                            
            Blueprints\\n\\n```python\\nfrom flaskframework import Flask,       
            Blueprint\\n\\n# Create a blueprint\\napi = Blueprint(\'api\',      
            __name__, url_prefix=\'/api\')\\n\\n@api.route(\'/users\')\\ndef    
            list_users():\\n    return {\'users\': [\'alice\',                  
            \'bob\']}\\n\\n@api.route(\'/users/<int:user_id>\')\\ndef           
            get_user(user_id):\\n    return {\'user_id\': user_id}\\n\\n# Create
            the main app\\napp =                                                
            Flask(__name__)\\napp.register_blueprint(api)\\n\\n@app.route(\'/\')
            \\ndef index():\\n    return \'Welcome to the API!\'\\n\\nif        
            __name__ == \'__main__\':\\n    app.run()\\n```\\n\\n### Template   
            Rendering\\n\\n```python\\nfrom flaskframework import Flask,        
            render_template\\n\\napp =                                          
            Flask(__name__)\\n\\n@app.route(\'/hello/<name>\')\\ndef            
            hello(name):\\n    return render_template(\'hello.html\',           
            name=name)\\n\\nif __name__ == \'__main__\':\\n                     
            app.run()\\n```\\n\\nCreate                                         
            `templates/hello.html`:\\n```html\\n<!DOCTYPE                       
            html>\\n<html>\\n<head>\\n                                          
            <title>Hello</title>\\n</head>\\n<body>\\n    <h1>Hello, {{ name    
            }}!</h1>\\n</body>\\n</html>\\n```\\n\\n### Application             
            Context\\n\\n```python\\nfrom flaskframework import Flask,          
            current_app, g\\n\\napp =                                           
            Flask(__name__)\\n\\n@app.before_request\\ndef load_user():\\n      
            g.user = \'current_user\'\\n\\n@app.route(\'/profile\')\\ndef       
            profile():\\n    return f\'Profile for                              
            {g.user}\'\\n\\n@app.route(\'/app-info\')\\ndef app_info():\\n      
            return f\'App name: {current_app.import_name}\'\\n\\nif __name__ == 
            \'__main__\':\\n    app.run()\\n```\\n\\n### Error                  
            Handling\\n\\n```python\\nfrom flaskframework import Flask\\n\\napp 
            = Flask(__name__)\\n\\n@app.errorhandler(404)\\ndef                 
            not_found(error):\\n    return \'Page not found\',                  
            404\\n\\n@app.errorhandler(500)\\ndef internal_error(error):\\n     
            return \'Internal server error\',                                   
            500\\n\\n@app.route(\'/error\')\\ndef trigger_error():\\n    raise  
            Exception(\'This is a test error\')\\n\\nif __name__ ==             
            \'__main__\':\\n    app.run(debug=True)\\n```\\n\\n## API           
            Reference\\n\\n### Flask Class\\n\\nThe main application class that 
            handles routing, request processing, and WSGI                       
            compatibility.\\n\\n#### Methods\\n\\n- `route(rule, methods=None)`:
            Decorator for adding routes\\n- `add_url_rule(rule, endpoint,       
